    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\alpha=37^\\circ,\\quad\\beta=80^\\circ,\\quad\\gamma=20^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "Alternate angles across the diagonal give $\\alpha=37^\\circ$ from the horizontal parallel sides, and $\\beta=80^\\circ$ from the other parallel pair. In the lower-left triangle, $(3\\gamma+3)+37+80=180$. Hence $3\\gamma+3=63$, so $\\gamma=20^\\circ$.",
